<title>BELGIUM: EU buys 10,321 tonnes of beef for intervention.</title>
<headline>EU buys 10,321 tonnes of beef for intervention.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's beef management committee accepted a total of 10,321 tonnes of beef into intervention on Friday, a Commission spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Commission accepted more beef than expected due to low offer levels, the official added.</p>
<p>The maximum price was 273 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>Total offers amounted to 17,573 tonnes.</p>
<p>Commenting on the low level of tenders a Commission official said it reinforced the Commission's view that the EU beef market is returning to normal. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
